[69.144071,"o","   or: busybox --install [-s] [DIR]\n"]
[69.144088,"o","   or: function [arguments]...\n"]
[69.144104,"o","\n"]
[69.144121,"o","    BusyBox is a multi-call binary that combines many common Unix\n"]
[69.144138,"o","    utilities into a single executable.  Most people will create a\n"]
[69.144156,"o","    link to busybox for each function they wish to use and BusyBox\n"]
[69.144173,"o","    will act like whatever it was invoked as.\n"]
[69.144191,"o","\n"]
[69.144208,"o","Currently defined functions:\n"]
[69.144225,"o","    [, [[, adjtimex, ar, arp, arping, ash, awk, basename, blockdev, brctl,\n"]
